  "text": "Motion, motion, change in position of an object with time. Velocity, acceleration along a straight line. Common to everything in the universe, motion, motion. We walk, we ride a bicycle, we run, sleep, and air moves through the room. Blood flows in arteries and veins. Birds move your flares and the PUA king. Carry people, automobiles, and planes. Water flowing down a dam, leaves falling from trees. Earth rotates once every twenty-four hours, revolves around the sun once in a year. The sun in motion in the Milky Way, moving within its local group of galaxies. Rectilinear motion, uniform acceleration. A set of simple equations. Relative nature of motion, relative velocity. Point objects valid so far as size is much smaller than the distance it moves in a reasonable duration of time. Real life, good number of situations, size neglected without much error. Motion, motion, change in position of an object with time. Velocity, acceleration along a straight line.",
